# Pull requests

When opening PRs for this repository (including via `gh pr create`):

## Titles

- Use **conventional commits** style: `type(scope): short description` (same spirit as merge commits).
- Do **not** put **roadmap theme labels** or **unreleased product milestone numbers** in the title
  (for example avoid `v1.19`, `v1.18 portal`, `v1.25` as the feature name).
  Roadmap versions describe planning themes; GitHub **engine tags** (for example `v1.25.0`) come from
  semantic-release and may not match roadmap numbering.
- OK in titles: semver when it is the **actual artifact** being changed (for example
  `chore(release): 1.26.0` on Release automation PRs).

## Bodies

- Summarize user-visible behavior and link operator/portal/docs impacts when relevant.
- Test plan checklist; note if operator JSON contracts (`plan-upgrade`, `apply-upgrade`) are unchanged.

## Merging to `main`

After required checks pass, use the normal **Merge pull request** control on GitHub.
Release automation (`chore/release/*`) still admin-merges outside branch rules.
See [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md) and [`.github/rulesets/README.md`](../.github/rulesets/README.md).
